cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, cite it as below, together with the access date.
title: >-
  cline-sentinel: one Windows notification when a Cline turn ends
abstract: >-
  cline-sentinel reads the local Cline event database on Windows and sends one notification when a
  turn ends, fails, is aborted, or waits for a human. It does not notify on ordinary mid-run
  silence. The tool uses the Python standard library, opens the database read-only, and does not
  call a model, use the network, or rely on a hook or model memory.

  SCOPE -- this is part of the citation. Cline Desktop 0.0.48 exposes notification toggles, but its
  Windows notification path is blocked in the tested build; this is an independent fallback, not an
  official Cline feature. It supports Windows and the local Cline event database only. The database
  schema is a Cline implementation detail and may change. A notification proves that Windows
  accepted a call; it does not prove that a banner was displayed or seen. The guard has no layer
  below it. The approval-prompt path has not been separately verified.
authors:
  - family-names: "Chan"
    given-names: "Kingho"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-0435-2030"
type: software
version: "1.0.3"
date-released: "2026-11-02"
